            "body": "feat(boundary): HISO-005 BUILD0247 CJS export value in the B6 kernel (C0 handles, opaque initial exports, branch join)\n\nSPEC0247 (082ad2f4…), approved by the user on 2026-10-20 for a local BUILD.\n\n- C0: closed syntactic categories of the CommonJS wrapper handles\n  (FUNCTION_BODY_WRITE, REFUSED_CONTEXT_WRITE, MODULE_REFERENCE,\n  EXPORTS_REFERENCE, LOADER_REFERENCE, EVAL_REFERENCE, TOP_LEVEL_THIS,\n  TOP_LEVEL_ARGUMENTS, TOP_LEVEL_RETURN); one UNKNOWN_CJS_EXPORTS root per\n  category in the module, normal pass and census; any category gives U to\n  every importer, first load and cache.\n- C1: the tracked value of a CJS module starts as its opaque exports object\n  (identity per file), not undefined; checkExport emits nothing for it.\n- C2: after an undecided `if` in a CJS module the tracked value is the union\n  of the branch values (absent branch = value before the `if`).\n- C3: checkExport keeps running on the tracked value.\n- Kernel version semantic-kernel-v7-cjs-export-value; literal migrated in six\n  B6 tests. New test tests/b6-0247-cjs-export-value.test.js with the 71 SPEC\n  fixtures and the R2 review cases T1, T2, T2b, T3 and Q3.\n\nLimits, recipes, resolution profile and the global proof rule are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
